<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Dancing Rabbit Creek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Dancing Rabbit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> was signed on 27 September 1830 in Noxubee County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, the first removal treaty concluded under the Indian Removal Act. The Choctaw ceded about 11 million acres of their remaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> in exchange for land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a>. Most were removed west in hard journeys between 1831 and 1833, while some stayed in Mississippi under a clause offering individual land allotments.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-dancing-rabbit-creek.jpg" alt="Treaty of Dancing Rabbit Creek" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dancing-Rabbit-Creek.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
